# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
wheels/
*.egg-info

# uv.lock is intentionally NOT committed here. This repo was originally developed on a
# machine whose uv is globally configured to resolve packages through a Databricks-
# internal PyPI proxy (pypi-proxy.dev.databricks.com) rather than public pypi.org --
# every uv.lock generated there records that proxy as the package source, which is
# unreachable from outside Databricks' network. A public demo repo's checked-in lockfile
# pinning an unreachable internal registry would break `uv sync`/`uv run` for every
# external user (and did break it, silently, for this whole project's history, until a
# CI job actually exercised `uv sync` from outside that network). Leaving it uncommitted
# means each environment resolves fresh against whatever index it's actually configured
# for -- correct urls, just without commit-pinned exact versions.
uv.lock

# Virtual environments
.venv
venv/

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

